<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Welshpool</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Welshpool is a market town in Powys, mid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-severn">River Severn</a> and the English border. It grew up below the castle of the princes of Powys Wenwynwyn and received a borough charter in the 13th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/powis-castle">Powis Castle</a> stands on its edge, and the town remains a centre for the surrounding farming country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/welshpool.jpg" alt="Welshpool" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Kelly · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broad_Street,_Welshpool.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
